  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Family relationships",
     "texto": [
      "**Bunic** and **bunică** mean «grandfather» and «grandmother»; **verișor** and **verișoară**, «male cousin» and «female cousin». **Cumnat** and **cumnată** are «brother-in-law» and «sister-in-law»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The genitive",
     "texto": [
      "To say «whose», the possessed noun usually takes the article at the end and the family word changes: **sora mamei** («the mother's sister»). With feminine names such as Ana, **-ei** appears (**soțul Anei**); with masculine names **lui** is used (**fratele lui Paul**). Unlike English, no word like «of» is added."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
